+## 2026-10-23 — Supervisor review: partial candidate changes, validation blocked
+
+Reason: review the October 20 payment, unassociated event and withdrawal-fee feedback together with the October 23 handoff. The current working tree contains candidate changes to FAQ query preservation, scoped public event-search guidance, commission prompt scope, payment field semantics, probe phone preflight, and objective regression fixtures/cases. These are uncommitted and unaccepted; implementation is paused following the user's request for an agent-assisted consolidated plan.
+
+Decision: withdrawal fees and gift commissions remain distinct FAQ topics. The current candidate's withdrawal-calculator assertion is unsupported and must be replaced. The latest-request-only design also needs a returned-parked-request regression and request identity repair. Details and remaining work: `docs/plan/2026-10-23-consolidated-supervisor-audit/implementation-plan.md`.
+
+Validation: baseline focused checks passed 84/84. Candidate focused checks passed 128 with one skipped. Full offline run: 210 files passed, two failed; 1700 tests passed, two failed, one skipped. Both remaining failures are the extraction instruction budget; subsequent targeted checks still measured 6005 bytes against 6000. Typecheck and scoped lint rerun passed. Representative reply instruction/input byte measurements: missing-event 2383/1462; commission 1337/1550. Candidate build succeeded in `.artifacts/review-2026-10-23-build`. Development deployment stopped at STS because the AWS STS/sign-in endpoints were unreachable. No new live case, supervised conversation, deployed hash or paid run is claimed. Preserve all failures and existing untracked analysis; do not present historical live results as validation of these edits.
+
+## 2026-10-23 — Audit instruction consistency before prompt-size repair
+
+User correction: investigate contradictory instructions instead of optimizing characters. Built the actual established-support extraction spec locally (seven files; instructions 6005 bytes, input 1288 bytes; no model/network call). Found conflicting availability ownership, stale `destination_account` selector guidance absent from the extraction schema, and reply/disclosure guidance loaded into extraction without evidence scoping. Distinguished repeated credential protection and broad state-preservation wording from definite contradictions. Also confirmed the separate FAQ route/settlement inconsistency and withdrawal/commission topic-selection issue. Recorded repairs and validation criteria in `docs/plan/2026-10-23-consolidated-supervisor-audit/prompt-consistency-audit.md` and updated the consolidated plan. No runtime/prompt edits, threshold changes, deployment or paid evaluations in this pass.
+
+## 2026-10-23 — Whole-catalog audit and offline prompt review invalidation
+
+Reason: the user requested a wider audit and a sustainable prevention mechanism instead of prompt-character optimization, followed by a single local-thread handoff. Three parallel read-only reviewers inspected extractor/router, reply/shared/node prompts, and audit infrastructure. Catalog: 130 files; 86 have only retired/audit consumer descriptions. The existing audit passed 34 legacy bundle checks despite production composition, schema and policy contradictions; full findings are in the consolidated supervisor-audit folder.
+
+Decision: implemented a deterministic offline review-freshness gate (`src/audit/prompt-freshness.ts` and CLI), added `npm run audit:prompt-freshness` to `check` and CI, and generated a 130-file **pending** review lock. It fingerprints prompt content plus runtime/core/schema/compiler/tool and checked-in knowledge dependencies; file/dependency changes and unresolved review findings fail closed. Candidate generation cannot approve entries or overwrite a review. This is review invalidation, not automatic semantic proof. Typed module binding/invariant contracts, true production reachability and actual serialized-request matrix checks remain explicit implementation work for the local thread. No conversational behavior was changed in this wider-audit pass.
+
+Validation: new audit/freshness tests 20/20 across four files, including five freshness regressions; typecheck and scoped lint passed. Whole-catalog review check intentionally fails because 130 entries are pending; do not approve known conflicts merely to clear CI. Prior two 6005/6000-byte failures and unverified candidate behavioral cases remain visible. No AWS deployment, live/model call or paid run. Single entry point: `docs/plan/2026-10-23-consolidated-supervisor-audit/START-HERE.md`. All changes remain uncommitted; preserve the current tree and existing unrelated untracked analysis.
